-- title:
--   Finiteness of the four-generator roof over k(j,j_N)
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field and let $N$ and $q$ be natural numbers, both assumed nonzero. Inside the field of Laurent series $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ k$ consider the intermediate field $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldC}\ k\ N$, defined as the $k$-subextension generated by the two elements $\mathtt{jqModC}\ k$ and $\mathtt{jqNModC}\ k\ N$, and the larger intermediate field $\mathtt{charLDegeneracyRoof}\ k\ N\ q$, defined as the $k$-subextension generated by the four elements $\mathtt{jqModC}\ k$, $\mathtt{jqNModC}\ k\ N$, $\mathtt{jqNModC}\ k\ q$ and $\mathtt{jqNModC}\ k\ (N q)$. The map $\mathtt{heckeAlphaC}\ k\ N\ q$ is the inclusion of the former into the latter, a $k$-algebra homomorphism. The assertion is $\mathtt{AlgebraicCurve.FiniteAlong}$ for this map: equipping the roof field with the algebra structure over $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldC}\ k\ N$ transported along the inclusion, the roof field is a finite module over $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldC}\ k\ N$, i.e. the extension $k(\mathtt{jqModC},\mathtt{jqNModC}\,N) \subseteq k(\mathtt{jqModC},\mathtt{jqNModC}\,N,\mathtt{jqNModC}\,q,\mathtt{jqNModC}\,(Nq))$ is finite. No primality is imposed on $q$, and no hypothesis is placed on the characteristic of $k$.
--
--   This is the finiteness half of the classical statement that the generators of the modular function fields of composite level satisfy monic modular equations over $k(j)$ (Kronecker's modular equation), here in the form that the degeneracy roof field attached to levels $N$, $q$ and $Nq$ is a finite extension of the level-$N$ field. It supplies the finiteness input required to form degeneracy correspondences and Hecke operators on the modular curve of level $N$, and to invoke the fundamental identity and the pushforward norm formula for the associated morphisms of curves.
